WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.389
[MUSIC]

00:00:01.389 --> 00:00:02.211
Hi.

00:00:02.211 --> 00:00:04.079
This is Jenny.

00:00:04.079 --> 00:00:06.273
She's a robotic emotional support animal.

00:00:06.273 --> 00:00:07.043
&gt;&gt; What a girl.

00:00:07.043 --> 00:00:07.583
What a good girl.
&gt;&gt; And

00:00:07.583 --> 00:00:09.419
she's designed to help
keep seniors company.

00:00:09.419 --> 00:00:11.297
&gt;&gt; Good girl.

00:00:11.297 --> 00:00:13.007
Good girl.

00:00:13.007 --> 00:00:14.730
&gt;&gt; My name is Tom Stevens.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.240
I am CEO and co-founder of Tombot.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.990
My mother raised me around animals.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.852
We had horses as pets in the backyard,
along with ducks, chicken,

00:00:24.852 --> 00:00:28.750
geese and dogs and cats, and so
I was raised around animals and

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.800
animals played a special role not only
in my life but in my mothers life.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.770
After my mother was
diagnosed with Alzheimer's,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:42.240
by far the worst day was taking away
her dog, my mother was devastated.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.250
And it broke my heart to be the one to
have to take her dog away from her.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.543
That launched me on
a multi-year research and

00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:51.791
education effort to solve my
mother's problems specifically.

00:00:51.791 --> 00:00:56.030
I received my Master's in science
from Stanford Business School.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.015
The biggest thing I took away from the MSX
program were really the relationships that

00:01:00.015 --> 00:01:02.480
I formed with the other
members of our cohort.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.780
I came to love and respect the people that
had many years under their career and

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:10.650
could provide me their insights.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:15.605
When a senior is diagnosed with
Alzheimer's or another causal disease for

00:01:15.605 --> 00:01:18.735
dementia, they begin losing
things in their lives.

00:01:18.735 --> 00:01:23.525
Where a senior can form a robust emotional
attachment to an object, traditionally

00:01:23.525 --> 00:01:27.895
human baby dolls or stuffed animals, that
senior gets a great deal of relief and

00:01:27.895 --> 00:01:31.165
the tech world, my roots,
fairly ignored this.

00:01:31.165 --> 00:01:36.220
So what we set out to do is build
a better emotional attachment object.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:40.060
Jenny is a fully interactive,
robotic emotional support animal.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.670
She's covered with sensors, she can feel
how and where she's being touched and

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:48.980
respond in a manner that's consistent
with how a live animal would respond.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:53.090
By caring for the robot they
again have a sense of purpose,

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.980
where the well being of the robot
becomes a focal point in their lives.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.380
The largest struggles have
really been around fundraising.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.086
We ran a Kickstarter campaign.

00:02:02.086 --> 00:02:05.160
The goal for the Kickstarter was
really to build awareness and

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.180
to test the market to see what
kind of response we received.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:12.973
We received overwhelming response
from seniors with dementia to parents

00:02:12.973 --> 00:02:16.927
of children with autism to doctors and
nurses in hospitals.

00:02:16.927 --> 00:02:21.104
And it was through that that we realized
that we were going to be able to build

00:02:21.104 --> 00:02:24.198
a fairly robust community
surrounding our product.

00:02:24.198 --> 00:02:27.060
My mother passed away in October of 2018,
and

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.020
she was actually
the inspiration behind the name.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.400
She just asked me,
what are you going to name the company?

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.780
I said, well, I'm not sure.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.230
She said, well, how about Tom?

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:38.070
That led us to call it Tombot.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:42.596
So every day when the company's name
is used, I think back to my mother and

00:02:42.596 --> 00:02:46.100
all of the wonderful work that
she did with us to help us get

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.992
our products to a place where they were
useful and purposeful for other people.

00:02:50.992 --> 00:02:59.861
[MUSIC]

